.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-auth-status 1  "rev-stealth-auth-status " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-auth\-status \- Report freshness/expiry status for a profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth auth status\fR <\fB\-\-profile\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report freshness / expiry status for the given profile. Returns exit 4 when the stored profile is expired or empty, so callers can distinguish refresh\-needed from hard failures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth auth status \-\-profile work
  $ rev\-stealth \-\-format json auth status \-\-profile work

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Profile is fresh.
  1  UserError        Bad args / unknown profile.
  3  PermanentError   AuthStore unavailable.
  4  AuthExpired      Profile expired / unusable.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTH_DIR        Override the AuthStore directory.
